/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-05T23:35:57Z","updated_at":"2025-06-05T23:35:57Z","body":"> As I said above, I'm not at all convinced we should expose the same functionality twice. If it's alright with everyone, I'd like to discuss this at the core meeting next Wednesday.\r\n\r\nYes, let's discuss. We definitely shouldn't be exposing an API \"for consistency\" with an internal API when we don't even have consensus on the internal API","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2946941537/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2948012008","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107141#issuecomment-2948012008","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107141","id":2948012008,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6vtxfo","user":{"login":"beicause","id":75941842,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1OTQxODQy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75941842?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause","html_url":"https://github.com/beicause","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beicause/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-06T04:00:49Z","updated_at":"2025-06-06T04:24:50Z","body":"In C# Rid is a separate wrapper and `IsValid` is a property.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/5dd76968d802f62a4933a604d40b68f321ae1ef1/modules/mono/glue/GodotSharp/GodotSharp/Core/Rid.cs#L46\r\n\r\nI agree `is_null` is just a internal code style of Godot and it is not necessary, and `Rid.IsNull` might confuse me because there's also nullable Rid (`Rid?`) in C#. For example: `if( rid != null ) if( rid.IsNull ) {} ` isn't clearer than `!rid.IsValid`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2948012008/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2951117289","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107141#issuecomment-2951117289","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107141","id":2951117289,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6v5nnp","user":{"login":"aaronfranke","id":1646875,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDY4NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1646875?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke","html_url":"https://github.com/aaronfranke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https